      "body": [
        "OpenTelemetry is a framework for collecting traces, the connected records of operations in a software request. A telemetry.dev guide applies it to AI agents that run from message queues. When a producer sends work to a queue and a worker later picks it up, the agent's model and tool calls can appear as a disconnected trace if the message does not carry the original context.",
        "The guide recommends first injecting trace context into each message's metadata while a producer span, a record of an operation, is active. The consumer then extracts the context separately for each message. For a batch, it links the receive span to each message context: one span cannot have multiple parents. Each message gets its own process span parented to its extracted context, with the agent run beneath it. The article recommends checking a batch of at least three messages in a trace viewer, because a single message can hide an incorrect batch parent. It also advises keeping prompts and secrets out of message metadata and checking for stripped headers or sampling when traces are missing."
